ent (52 °C for 2 hours) for seed material.\n\n*Monitoring advice*  \n- Inspect the stalks weekly for red rot signs (cankered, rotting internodes).  \n- Look for smut “whip” sori (black, elongated structures) emerging from the growing point.  \n- Check leaves for rust pustules (orange‑red specks) and leaf‑spot lesions (brown or dark spots).  \n- Record any new symptoms with date and location in the field.\n\n*When to seek expert help*  \n- If any of the above symptoms appear on more than a few plants.  \n- If disease spreads rapidly despite the above preventive steps.  \n- If you need assistance with hot‑water treatment or selection of resistant varieties.\n\n(Full fact-checking was unavailable for this answer; only the local number and name checks ran.)", "fact_check": "skipped", "fact_check_seconds": 0.0, "groq_calls": [{"purpose": "rewrite", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": null, "completion_tokens": null, "seconds": 0.0, "status": "skipped", "seq": 9}, {"purpose": "answer", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "prompt_tokens": 1808, "completion_tokens": 1067, "seconds": 3.63, "status": "ok", "seq": 10}, {"purpose": "fact_check", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": null, "completion_tokens": null, "seconds": 0.0, "status": "skipped", "seq": 11}]}
